Just so you know, teaching your pet to steal requires, IIRC, 'a treat'.
 In cats/dogs case, they are tripe rations, meatballs, and maybe chunks
of meat, if you can lift it and throw it.  I am not 100% on the list of
the treats, so don't quote me on that one, but you can't teach them to
steal with any food they eat.  Throwing a corpse won't do that.

On the other hand, taming does, and it does indeed depends on whether
they actually successfully catch it.  I've had some misfires before as
well, and yes, sometimes you do end up hurting the target.  Also, note
that the food they eat without being hungry and food they eat when they
are hungry are different.  Your pets won't eat human food (rations,
etcs) if they aren't hungry, but even horses eat human food when they
are hungry and if you throw the food at them.

